title: The Right is angry!
subtitle: We have angered our coalition partners too much...
new-page: true
on-arrival: tried_supporting_kpd = 0; weimar_dissent += 1 if weimar_plan_adopted
view-if: (((chancellor_party != "SPD" and chancellor_party != "KPD" and spd_in_government = 1 and ((in_grand_coalition = 1 or in_popular_front = 1 or in_minority_government = 1) and coalition_dissent >= 3)) or (in_weimar_coalition = 1 and coalition_dissent >= 4 and spd_r < 50)) and violence_timer > 0)
tags: event


= Breaking point

Dissent has consumed our coalition, with some in the right advocating to splinter off and negotiate with the far right. Although, due to our circumstances, our coalition cannot break off, so we are forced to the negotiating table.

The Z demands that we work with the military, citing that a this point, the country is bound to head for a civil war.

The military demands that we demands that we should work on deescalating the conflict through all paramilitaries de militarizing with them as a mediator.

[? if dvp_in_government : The DVP demands that we should work on deescalating the conflict through all paramilitaries de militarizing with the military as a mediator, for a sort of deescalation. ?]

What should we do?

- @wirth: Joseph Wirth can enforce party discipline 
- @military: We are forced to give more concessions to the military. 
- @deescalation: hmmm, RFB dominance.
- @accelerate: Promise that we will crush the paramilitaries immediately, and that we will accelerate the time we will accomplish this
- @itsover: We have no choice, the military shall assume full control over the government.

@wirth
subtitle: By begging Wirth to convince his party to change their minds, we can stave off a vote of no confidence. This will damage his position within the Center.
choose-if: wirth_ascendant
on-arrival: coalition_dissent -= 2

Wirth is too goated.

@military
subtitle: [? if military_concessions == 4 : If we give them anymore concessions, we will get couped. ?] [? if military_concessions == 0 : -1 budget ?] [? if military_concessions == 2 : -2 budget ?]
on-arrival: military_concessions += 2; budget -=1 if military_concessions == 0; budget -= 2 if military_concessions == 2; coalition_dissent = 0; {!

if (Q.military_concessions == 1) {
    Q.reichswehr_loyalty += 0.05;
    Q.workers_spd -= 3;
    Q.unemployed_spd -= 3;
    Q.workers_nsdap += 3;
    Q.unemployed_kpd += 3;
    Q.month_actions += 1;
}

if (Q.military_concessions == 2) {
    Q.reichswehr_loyalty += 0.4;
    Q.budget -= 1;
    Q.reichswehr_strength += 100;
    Q.left_dissent += 10;
    Q.month_actions += 1;
}

if (Q.military_concessions == 3) {
    Q.reichswehr_loyalty += 0.25;
    Q.rb_dissent += 25;
    Q.month_actions += 1;
}

if (Q.military_concessions == 4) {
    Q.reichswehr_loyalty += 0.4;
    Q.budget -= 2;
    Q.reichswehr_militancy += 1;
    Q.reichswehr_strength += 200;
    Q.left_dissent += 25;
    Q.month_actions += 1;
}

if (Q.military_concessions == 5) {
    Q.reichswehr_loyalty += 0.3;
    Q.rb_dissent = 100;
    Q.month_actions += 1;
}

!}

[? if military_concessions == 1 : We promise the army to fund them once this is over. A vague promise of future military funding. It buys us time, but at the cost of slight credibility. ?]

[? if military_concessions == 2 : We allocate a part of their budget to placate them. The left our party are irritated. They cite it shows weakness, and could start a trend of once again, going to the military for help.?]

[? if military_concessions == 3 : We can delegate some of our paramilitary suppression operations to the Reichswehr. The Reichsbanner are untrusting of the Reichswehr, yet for now at least, most tolerate their presence.?]

[? if military_concessions == 4 : We can allocate a large portion of our budget on militarizing the Reichswehr even further. The left's fear have only grown worse, with many hardliners leaving the party and joining the KPD! Many in the party are starting to doubt our actions. ?]

[? if military_concessions == 5 : We can give up major positions on anti streetfighting operations. The Reichsbanner are absolutely pissed ?]

@accelerate
subtitle: This effectively halves our time that we have, in addition, the military will start to grow weary month by month.
view-if: violence_acceleration == 0
on-arrival: violence_acceleration = 1; violence_timer /= 2; coalition_dissent = 0

This is a risky decision, and we may not be up to the task. At least we didn't have to give any concessions.

@itsover
view-if: military_concessions == 4 and wirth_ascendant != 1 and violence_acceleration

- @game_over: Game over.